    "description": "I currently manage the Integrator and Cramer Inventory systems development team - consisting of approximately 30 employees/contractors who report directly to me. Integrator is a suite of applications primarily written in the Smalltalk language (CINCOM Visual Works) which provides data networking inventory, provisioning, element alarm handling and ticketing sevices. Integrator inventories ATM, FR, MOE, TLS and DSL Subscriber services. Cramer is a COT (off the shelf/inventory framework) selected by Qwest to serve as the inventory system for the next generation of packet level services. I also participate as embedded architect for both systems.\nI have developed software in Smalltalk for 14 years. I have also develop distributed software using Java, Weblogic, Tibco and other technologies.",
